
# The Pages workflow checks the codecave.pro repo out here for its build
# toolchain. CI-only, but ignored so a local reproduction of the workflow does
# not offer to commit someone else's repository.
/_toolchain/

# ds-bundle/ STOPPED being an upload staging directory on 2026-08-27. It held 46
# gitignored byte-for-byte copies of files that already existed under src/ and
# docs/, materialized before every push by tools/build-ds-bundle.sh and then
# verified against their originals by 40 lines of that same script.
#
# None of it was ever required. DesignSync's write_files takes the project path
# and the local path as INDEPENDENT arguments, so the upload is a list of
# source-to-destination pairs and never needed a directory to mirror.
# tools/design-sync-map.mjs is that list now, and the copies are gone.
#
# What remains gitignored is one thing, and it is GENERATED rather than copied:
# the seven Components cards, written by tools/build-ds-components.mjs from its
# own tracked STORIES table. They have no other home, so they are written here
# and uploaded from here.
ds-bundle/components/Components/

# AUTHORED — tracked, and deliberately not listed here: README.md, styles.css,
# guidelines/brand.md, and components/Foundations/*/*.html. Those seven files
# exist nowhere else in this repo and nothing regenerates them. Under the old
# blanket rule they were untracked source: invisible to review and one `rm -rf`
# from gone.

# Internal planning, kept on disk and out of the published repository. Jira is
# the system of record for open work. TODO.md was the staging area in front of
# it and is now gone — its six items were filed as CCWEB2-314..317 (label
# `brand-kit`) or closed out, and CLAUDE.md carries the index so an empty repo
# is never mistaken for an empty backlog.
#
# WEBSITE-REVIEW.md is NOT here on purpose: twelve places cite it, three of them
# comments inside the shipped colors_and_type.css, and README.md opens with a
# promise about it. It goes only when those citations point at Jira instead.
/TODO.md

# The npm package (CCWEB2-318). packages/brand/ is a PURE DERIVATIVE of docs/:
# every byte it publishes is copied or compiled from there, so none of its
# output is source and none of it is tracked. `npm run check` asserts the
# derivation still holds; package-lock.json IS tracked, because a lockfile is
# the only thing making the build reproducible.
node_modules/

# Produced by `npm run build:storybook` from src/components/ and src/captured/,
# on the same rule as packages/*/dist/ and /dist/: src/ is authored, everything
# else is generated. They were tracked until 2026-08-27, guarded by a sha256 of
# the component roots recorded in the tw-bridge.css header -- an arrangement
# that existed only because the generator once needed a codecave.pro checkout
# and so could not run everywhere. It runs anywhere now, and CI already
# rebuilt these and published the fresh output rather than the committed one,
# so the check was failing builds over files the same run discarded.
docs/storybook/compiled/
docs/storybook/tw-bridge.css
packages/*/dist/
packages/*/.tmp/

# The docs site (CCWEB2-317). `dist/` is docs/ passed through with the .astro
# pages rendered over the top, and it is rebuilt from a clean checkout on every
# deploy — committing it would put generated noise in every diff, which is the
# whole reason the build does NOT write back into docs/. `.astro/` is the type
# cache Astro regenerates on demand.
#
# Note the asymmetry with the rule above: packages/*/dist/ is ignored because
# nothing there is source, and /dist/ is ignored for the same reason. docs/
# stays committed because it is the origin for both of them.
/dist/
/.astro/

# Copied from the root LICENSE at build time. npm only picks a licence up from
# the package root, and the root file is the origin — see scripts/build.mjs.
packages/*/LICENSE

# `npm pack` output. RELEASING.md step 3 asks for one so the tarball can be
# installed and smoke-tested before tagging, and it lands wherever it was run.
# The release itself packs its own on the runner and never sees a local copy, so
# nothing here is ever an input to anything — but `npm publish <file.tgz>` is a
# real command, and a stale tarball committed to the tree is something someone
# would eventually reach for.
*.tgz

# The package build takes this while it holds .tmp and dist/. It exists
# because a watcher makes two concurrent builds ordinary rather than exotic --
# see the lock in packages/brand/scripts/build.mjs. Removed on exit, stolen if
# the process that wrote it is gone.
packages/*/.build.lock
